# OpenClaw State Persistence Fix

**Date:** February 15, 2026

## What happened

OpenClaw instances were writing session data and chat history to temporary storage instead of the persistent disk. When pods restarted (due to maintenance or scaling), all conversations and settings were lost. Gateway tokens also regenerated on restart, disconnecting active sessions.

## What we fixed

- All state now writes to persistent storage — sessions, conversations, and config survive pod restarts
- Gateway tokens are persisted and reused across restarts — no more random disconnections
- Frontend now detects disconnections and shows a reconnect button

## Action required

**You need to deploy a new OpenClaw instance.** Existing deployments run the old image and cannot be patched in place.

1. Delete your current OpenClaw deployment from the dashboard
2. Deploy a new one — it will use the fixed image automatically

Existing session history cannot be recovered.

## Affected?

If you lost important data or experienced repeated disconnections, please reach out for **credits**:

- Discord: Basilica server (https://discord.gg/uqAtYdYE)

