1472746526244737301,1354089114189955102,ᚠ・grail・81,799672011265015819,396796852948697090,mhi.erfan,Oriea,"You know! In this subnet at least, we've already built the initial building blocks to get rid of most of the exploits, but focusing mainly on making the system bullet proof especially as it is evolving all the time is not that much practical in our case. We prefer to spend most of our resources on improving the training pipeline for ther model rather than Pen Testing our system all the time to find the edge cases.

So right now, the responsibility for pen testing is given to the miners as <@1213176263758319698> mentioned.

Also I assume that you just joined this network. There were months and weeks before that system kept working without any exploits so it's not like we're gonna get exploited all the time. 

Also even in the case of this exploit, we already predicted it and implemented a super efficient cross miner duplication checker 4 months ago. The only thing we needed to adjust was failure threshold. If you look at the the new version nothing else has changed.",2026-02-16T00:08:54.164000+00:00,,False,1472679450872381450,False,0,0,0
1472747166584799366,1354089114189955102,ᚠ・grail・81,799672011265015819,396796852948697090,mhi.erfan,Oriea,"There are still some exploits that I think there's a chance that people can come up with. For instance, right now we do exact check between rollouts and we don't do character edit distance checks. Someone can come up with a new algo to change one or two characters in the rollout and then duplicate it. (the reason being that character edit distance checks can end up being super expensive even if we use efficient algorithms and result in some false positives because sometimes rollouts only different with a few characters during generation)

However, this require extensive pen testing in itself to make sure it's exploitable. The reason being is that if you change even one character in llms, the distribution checks are not gonna pass because the distribution for the rest of the characters can get screwed up. So I'm waiting for another person to potentially exploit that and a couple of other scenarios I have in mind!",2026-02-16T00:11:26.833000+00:00,2026-02-16T17:49:47.212000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,1
