1472977432909971736,1300553352274382848,ذ・bitsec・60,799672011265015819,263544733442244609,yubo,yubo,"we're turning off miner emissions. the top agents generated have limited utility for paying customers, bug bounties, or audit competitions.

this current IM design is broken and not rewarding the right actions. it's my fault and it sucks to realize this. we got a few good innovations like file rerank, reducing false positives, ranking vulnerabilities, but the bottom line is we're not getting what we need, and doing a few small tweaks will not get us there.

the plan going forward
- we're continuing to develop our claude code and codex workflows and running experiments on bug bounties / audit challenges / paid customers.
- redesign IM for v3. i don't know how long this will take, but the idea is to share our claude code / codex process, and miners compete to improve what we have shown works.

there are three key ideas with v3:
- make it closer to running claude code. we're evaluating platform cortex cli, opencode. miners will submit a collection of files with more advanced features. this should lead to more useful outputs.
- expand project set and randomize eval set. we'll expand scabench project set to hundreds, so it is harder to overfit, and internally test commercial viability on audit challenges, bug bounty code bases.
- innovations will get financial rewards beyond subnet emissions (direct portion of bug bounties, etc)",2026-02-16T15:26:26.603000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,0
