1473576936155644038,1387865673690251445,מ・basilica・39,799672011265015819,862337957972934657,itzlambda,itzlambda,"# Miner Config Migration Guide

We've shipped a new miner-initiated bidding model. Currently we have static strategy so miner will start and bid a certain price for each GPU category. In future we will allow miners to hook their own custom bidding logic.
 
Here's what you need to change in your miner.toml:

1. Remove [validator_comms] — this entire section is gone. Delete it.
⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨```diff
- [validator_comms]
- host = ""0.0.0.0""
- port = 50051
```⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩

2. Update your node entries — replace hourly_rate_per_gpu with gpu_category and gpu_count:
⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨```diff
[node_management]
nodes = [
-   { host = ""1.2.3.4"", port = 22, username = ""basilica"", hourly_rate_per_gpu = 2.50 },
+   { host = ""1.2.3.4"", port = 22, username = ""basilica"", gpu_category = ""H100"", gpu_count = 8 },
]
```⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩

3. Add the new [bidding] section — pricing is now per GPU category:
⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨```diff
+[bidding.strategy.static.static_prices]
+H100 = 2.50   # $/hour per GPU
+A100 = 1.20
```⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩

Every gpu_category in your nodes must have a matching price here or the miner won't start.
⁩⁩
4. Port config moved (if you customized it), use axon_port under [bittensor] instead:
⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨⁨```diff
+[bittensor]
+axon_port = 50051
```⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩⁩",2026-02-18T07:08:39.315000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,1
1473576987179352126,1387865673690251445,מ・basilica・39,799672011265015819,862337957972934657,itzlambda,itzlambda,"# Important  

Removing nodes the right way: Under the new model, you are responsible for properly withdrawing your nodes before taking them offline. If a node goes dark without being removed first, the validator will treat it as misbehavior. Misbehavior history will be factored into future rental selection, so nodes with a track record of going offline unexpectedly will be less likely to get rented.

To remove a node:
1. Check that the node has no active rental running on it. If it does, wait for the rental to complete first.
2. Remove the node from the nodes list in your miner.toml.
3. Restart the miner. On startup it will re-register with only the remaining nodes, which automatically stops the bid on the removed one.

If you remove a node while a rental is still active, the bid will be stopped but the rental will keep running, and the node going offline mid-rental counts as misbehavior.

Full updated docs: https://github.com/one-covenant/basilica/blob/main/docs/miner.md",2026-02-18T07:08:51.480000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,1
