1473590145230831676,1300553352274382848,ذ・bitsec・60,799672011265015819,1213176263758319698,formalised_tensor,distributed_tensor | covenant.ai,"> 3. Efficiency modifiers push toward production-readiness — without excluding premium agents. By including speed, cost, and false-positive rate as scoring modifiers, V3 signals that production efficiency matters. But critically, these are Tier 2 tie-breakers, not hard requirements. An agent that finds every bug at premium cost ($200/run, 4 hours) will still rank above a cheap agent that misses vulnerabilities — because detection rate dominates. The efficiency modifiers only separate agents at the same detection tier. This means the subnet naturally produces both ends of the market: premium thoroughness-maximising agents and lean cost-efficient ones. A commercial offering built on the subnet could serve different customer segments — a fast, cheap agent for CI/CD triage and a slow, expensive one for pre-deployment deep audits — all emerging from the same competitive pressure.

