1474063416430825617,1386721120652361800,𑀃・poker44・126,799672011265015819,1435366962153656420,sachhp,sachp,"**Introducing **Poker44** | Subnet 126 $TAO **

Poker44 was born from a simple conviction: **integrity** shouldn’t depend on **trust**. It should depend on things you can **verify**. 

This is why we are building a decentralized & open-source poker platform with world-class bot detection.

**🎯 Why are we building?**

Online poker has a **bot problem**. That part isn’t controversial anymore. What’s changed is how good they’ve gotten: timing that looks human, adaptive betting patterns, real-time assistance, and behavior that’s increasingly hard to distinguish from real players.
Meanwhile, players are still asked to “**just trust**”:
- that the shuffle is fair
- that private cards stay private
- that payouts are correct
- that detection is actually working

Most of that happens behind closed doors. Poker44 is an attempt to move those trust assumptions into verifiable systems.

**🛠 What are we building?**

**1) Bot detection powered by miners 🤖**
Bot detection won’t be handled privately by the platform. It’s evaluated openly as a subnet: miners submit detection models, validators score them on structured gameplay data, and performance is weighted on-chain. No “trust us, it works.” Results are measurable.

**2) Decentralized + verifiable + private execution (TEE) 🔐**
The game runtime runs inside an attested Trusted Execution Environment. That means people can verify what code is running, and the infrastructure hosting it can’t peek into sensitive game state (hole cards, randomness, internal logic). Verification is one side; privacy is the other.

**3) Verifiable settlement 📜**
Gameplay stays off-chain for latency, but balances settle on-chain through contracts using messages signed by the attested runtime. The goal is to reduce blind trust as much as possible without making the game unusable.

**🧪 Environments**

Real games are human-only by default. No hidden house bots, no silent experiments inside production. If bots exist, they run only in clearly labeled environments designed specifically for evaluation and data generation.

**⚔️ Why an adversarial loop (GANs)?**

Detecting bots isn’t a one-time ML task, it’s an arms race. So we’re designing a hybrid evaluation mode where increasingly human-like bots are developed **only for testing**, not for real-money deployment.
The point is to generate high-signal data and force continuous improvement:
as bots improve, detectors must improve;
as detectors improve, bots get pushed harder.
Controlled, explicit, and never mixed into real games.

**🌐 Why a decentralized platform?**

Because closed systems drift. Bots evolve, strategies evolve, incentives evolve, and private detection stacks tend to become “trust us” over time.

Bittensor gives an open competitive arena with objective validation and economic incentives tied to demonstrated performance, not claims.

Poker44 isn’t built on promises.
It’s built on **verifiability, privacy, and ongoing competition**. If this resonates, follow along, I’ll keep sharing progress as we build.

**The time has come. 
Poker44 is live.**

**♠️Prepare your chips ♠️**

