1474201161211973740,1247680967225905273,י・mind・34,799672011265015819,473634651995635722,kenobijon,Kenobi | BitMind,"## Details regarding Video Dynamic Frame Sampling 📽️ 

Models can now specify num_frames and frame_rate in their `model_config.yaml` to control how frames are sampled during inference:
```
preprocessing:  
resize: [224, 224]  # Alreayd existing
num_frames: 16  
frame_rate: 8.0    # sample at 8fps → 16 frames covers 2s of video
```

## What this means for you:
- You're no longer locked into the first 16 sequential frames, you can now control temporal coverage.
- `frame_rate` sets the sampling fps (e.g., 8.0 = one frame every 125ms). Defaults to native video frame rate, 8.0 if omitted from both. (Still 1 PR here) 
- `num_frames` sets how many frames are extracted. Defaults to 16 if omitted.
- If your model's input shape already encodes the frame count ([B, T, C, H, W]), it will be picked up automatically.
- If you don't change anything, the defaults will grab the same 16 frames as done with previous competition versions",2026-02-20T00:29:06.166000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,1
