1474309319523831943,1429935142847381617,დ・plaτform・100,799672011265015819,1118493701405163611,cortextao,"Echo | cortex.foundation [τ, დ]","<@&1432376959337238659> 

We will be able to release the **alpha version of the IDE today**. Miners will **no longer be incentivized** to find bugs in CortexLM/cortex, we are going to **redefine the incentive system** for bounty challenge. We will reduce agent activity and instead focus on **rewarding human work**. It's up to you to find the way to discover bugs. From now on, you will need to submit **videos and screenshots** of bugs you find on the IDE and on Cortex. Cortex will be **temporarily disabled** for bounty challenge as we are going to do a **major refactor of the CLI**.

The IDE will be released in alpha version today. There are **a lot of bugs**, and you'll need to find them all. It is **not production-ready** as planned, I'm counting on the miners' help to find all the IDE bugs.

Tonight we will release the IDE version on **CortexLM/cortex-ide**, we need all your reports. Report all bugs through bounty challenge so that you get **rewarded for helping us**. Bounty challenge will increase with a cap at **50% of emissions**, term challenge at **50% of emissions** as well, **no more burn**.

We want to incentivize as many miners as possible to mine on the subnet. Regarding bounty challenge, the 50% of emissions will be the __maximum emissions__. There will be a system that **increases emissions based on the number of bugs reported**, to prevent a single miner from staying at 100% of emissions by only reporting one bug. **Duplicate bugs will be drastically penalized**, since issues will for the most part no longer be 100% AI-assisted (unless you develop your own harness that tests the software via MCP and screenshots all the bugs, which I **highly recommend** you do. __Always stay one step ahead of the other miners__).

The plan is as follows. We are entering the **public alpha period**. CortexLM/cortex and CortexLM/cortex-ide are currently under development for a **production release in March**. No specific date for now.

For Cortex IDE, we will create a branch dedicated to **migrating everything from Tauri** and **getting rid of JavaScript entirely**. This will take time, but it will be a branch available for testing as well. This will allow us to fully harness 100% of your GPU performance and keep the IDE lightweight.

We also have a **redesign of the cortex.foundation website** coming in the next few weeks. You will be able to **launch multi-agents**, develop projects directly from the website, and be connected to the CLI or the IDE. We have a long-term vision and we are focused on **multi-agent orchestration**. We run a lot of tests regularly and have learned a great deal.

**__We can't wait to release the IDE to you.__** It will be available **tonight**, I'll make an announcement.",2026-02-20T07:38:53.117000+00:00,2026-02-20T08:39:23.071000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,7
