1474329342359244873,1386721120652361800,𑀃・poker44・126,799672011265015819,1435366962153656420,sachhp,sachp,"The platform we’ve built is an important starting point for the project. It will be open to everyone and we will organize free tournaments with incentives for the winners.
All gameplay data is stored in a structured way: response times, betting patterns, bet sizing, action sequences, contextual hand information, and other relevant parameters. This gives miners meaningful behavioral data to work with when training and refining their detection models, not just final outcomes, but how decisions are made.

In a later phase (around 2-3 weeks), we will **integrate bots directly into the platform**, exclusively within the hybrid mode. This will allow us to move much closer to the target dataset we’re aiming for: one where human hands and bot hands play at the same table in a controlled environment. Human participation will be incentivized through rewards when they win ensuring that the data generated remains competitive and high-signal

This represents an initial version of the system. **In parallel, we are building the decentralized architecture** .In that model, the game table will run on validator infrastructure rather than a traditional centralized server, inside an attested environment (TEE). This ensures that execution is verifiable and that sensitive state- private cards, randomness seeds, internal logic- remains protected even from the host itself.

We are also considering a **sub-subnet where miners compete to build human-like bots**, used exclusively in our training environment. This would create a GAN-style dynamic: one group of models generates realistic behavior, while another group detects it. As the bots improve, detection models submitted to validators must improve as well.
This adversarial setup forces continuous improvement and makes the detection layer progressively stronger.

Detection models will be evaluated on versioned, reproducible datasets with clearly defined performance metrics, including strict control of false positives. Weights will be assigned on-chain based on measurable results.

**The mid-term goal is a decentralized, open-source, and verifiable architecture** where game execution, model evaluation, and settlement all follow the same principle: reduce implicit trust and replace it with verifiable guarantees. 
I want to clarify something **important **about the objective of this subnet: it has** nothing to do with EVM, smart contracts, liquidity provision, or anything related to that.**

We’re building that transition step by step",2026-02-20T08:58:26.933000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,1
