1474875181531922605,1351180661918142474,و・loosh・78,799672011265015819,1339104482524528733,agentictoaster,AgenticToaster,"## Update on the recent Challenge API outage

Over the last few days we experienced an outage on our Challenge API caused by memory constraints, which prevented it from reliably receiving challenges from the inference gateway and relaying them to validators. I know this created uncertainty for validators and frustration for miners  and I appreciate everyone raising concerns quickly and clearly.

The important part: **the subnet’s safety mechanisms behaved as designed during the outage.** Validators successfully fell back to the emergency weight-setting path (the 4500-block safeguard), **weights continued to be set**, and **no miners were zeroed out** as a result of the service disruption. You can also see in the subnet portal’s weight distribution that weights are being applied.

### What we’re doing next (already in progress)
- Adding stronger **Prometheus metrics** across the stack
- **Log shipping into Grafana** with real-time dashboards
- **Server metrics shipping into Grafana** for CPU/mem/disk/network visibility
- **Real-time alerting** so we catch issues immediately and respond faster

### Ownership & responsiveness
I’m also introducing **<@1408546498689634316>**, who’s stepping in to own the subnet code and server stability end-to-end. Jeff will be focused on reliability, monitoring/alerting, and ensuring we’re more responsive when issues arise.

Thanks again for sticking with us. This is new tech and we’re moving quickly, but stability is the priority, and this incident is directly shaping how we harden the system from here.",2026-02-21T21:07:25.133000+00:00,2026-02-21T21:09:48.853000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,1
