1475414864246734870,1434923225229295697,ר・nepher・49,799672011265015819,1260100710649823252,nterprime,nτerprime | nepher.ai,"That makes sense. However, this approach requires additional consideration before implementation. The original design aimed to avoid inefficient resource usage.

Miners need time to train their policies, and when there are no new submissions, validators remain idle. This is not cost-effective and leads to unnecessary expenses.

We have already shared the evaluation repository and a sample dataset so miners can test their agents. They are also able to generate additional datasets for their own testing. If we provide frequent feedback based on benchmark results, there is a risk that their policies will become overfitted to the benchmark dataset.

We aim to give miners full flexibility. Whether their models are well-trained ultimately depends on their ability to create diverse datasets, fine-tune parameters, and apply effective training methodologies. This is also the reason why the evaluation period is isolated.

In any case, thank you for the valuable suggestion. We will take it into further consideration.",2026-02-23T08:51:55.519000+00:00,,False,1475213593732448388,False,0,0,0
