1475467544604184668,1434923225229295697,ר・nepher・49,799672011265015819,1260100710649823252,nterprime,nτerprime | nepher.ai,"📢 **Update Scheduled: Transition to Continuous Validation for Leatherback Task (Iteration 2)**
To foster a more competitive and transparent environment, we are evolving our evaluation logic. 

🔄 **The New Validation Workflow**
Currently, miners submit agents but no feedback until the end of the submit period. This makes miners keep blind during contest and submit period. So we are planning to split the evaluation into two distinct phases to balance live feedback with model integrity:

**• Phase 1: The Contest Period (Mock Evaluation)**
Live Leaderboard: A public leaderboard will be active throughout the contest.
Public Dataset: Evaluations will be performed using a Sample Dataset visible on the tournament website.
Goal: This allows you to debug your logic and see where you stand relative to other miners in real-time.
**• Phase 2: The Evaluation Period (Real Evaluation)**
Benchmark Dataset: Once the contest closes, models will be run against a Private Benchmark Dataset.
Final Ranking: Your final score and rewards will be determined exclusively by your performance on this private dataset.
Goal: To reward models that generalize well and avoid overfitting to the public samples.

⚖️** Why this change?**
This ""Double-Blind"" approach is a standard in world-class data science competitions. It ensures that the Live Leaderboard drives engagement and innovation, while the Private Benchmark ensures the final policy is robust, high-quality, and ready for real-world application.

🛠️ **What miners should do:**
Don't Overfit: A high rank on the Mock Leaderboard does not guarantee a win if your model is hard-coded to the sample data.
Cross-Validate: Use the public samples to build your pipeline, but rely on your own internal validation sets to ensure generalizability.
Monitor Live: Use the live feedback to iterate faster on your model architecture.

⏲️ **Timeline**
In a few days.

