1475517885844689017,1465362098971345010,ա・djinn・103,799672011265015819,551064429664403467,pmaymin,"Philip (Djinn, SN103)","Hmm let’s dig in.

TLSN timeouts are almost always one of these:

Notary server is slow/overloaded: we use notary.pse.dev:443 (PSE's public notary). It does an MPC-TLS handshake for every proof, which takes 30-60s even when healthy. If it's under load, it can exceed the 90s timeout.

Network connectivity: your miner needs fast, reliable outbound to both the notary server AND the target URL. High latency or packet loss will push you past the timeout.

Binary missing: if djinn-tlsn-prover isn't found in PATH, the miner silently falls back to HTTP attestation (weaker proof). Run which djinn-tlsn-prover to confirm it's installed.

No special env vars needed for attestation beyond the standard miner setup. The notary host/port default to notary.pse.dev:443 automatically.",2026-02-23T15:41:17.782000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,2
