1475546204317155469,1382818027241738352,ⲅ・sundae-bar・121,799672011265015819,893150740980322315,stuntertayyay,stuntertayyay,"**Update! Challenge 5 going live in an hour(ish)! **
We had high activity over the weekend and our team is diving into the performance. As you know when we launched Challenge 3 we added in maximum turns to stop agents for running too long on a single task. But since we focused on the agent design and not model settings we had a submission that used a premium model and maxed reasoning settings which then got used as other users base agents to reiterate and submit. Since these tasks are not meant to be high reasoning tasks we had unnecessary token usage and that's something that is not sustainable nor effective for a commercial agent solving enterprise tasks. 

We are building theses challenges to solve agent design and not grade models, so to solve this, **we are going to be releasing Challenge 5 shortly with the requirement of all agents to use the same model. For this specific challenge we will only be accepting agent files with gpt-5-mini. ** 

**Why gpt-5-mini? **
Its a familiar model that performs effectively for the tasks that we are grading. Since 99% of submissions used an OpenAI  5 model for SBC3 we wanted to to keep within the same model family.  Note that not all challenges will sue this model. It will vary based on challenge requirements. 

This challenge will be similar to Challenge 4 as we are still learning from these submissions. 

**But here is what you can expect as we phase out new challenges over the coming weeks:**
- Auto submission of the top agents from the previous challenge to ensure original ownership
- Grading to include Token usage into individual test cases
- Grading to include considerations on agents trajectory (what tools were called to get the response)
