1475695332854726853,1381987595881414656,ⴷ・ⴷffine・120,799672011265015819,1091660419023773828,bajibajicat,Tobias,"Two possible directions — both have trade-offs:

**Option 1: Enforce a Model Size Limit**

**Pros:**
• Forces participants to actually train / fine-tune instead of fully relying on large pretrained models

**Cons:**
• Parameter size verification is not trivial (int4 / int8 quantization, merged adapters, etc.) — could introduce loopholes
• Models trained under strict size limits may overfit to the benchmark
• Long-term general value of such models is uncertain

**Option 2: No Model Size Restriction**

**Pros:**
• More diverse solution space — unclear whether small-model full training or large-model LoRA will win long term
• Fewer constraints → lower system complexity
• Cleaner governance and easier implementation

**Cons:**
• Open-source foundation models may dominate the leaderboard for an extended period
• Could reduce incentives for deeper architectural innovatio",2026-02-24T03:26:24.446000+00:00,2026-02-24T03:26:41.615000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,1
