1476095770196185230,1349119225868058644,غ・vericore・70,799672011265015819,316899470723907585,mitchell_za,NeuroBYTE,"Hi <@1425862221321469994> 

The difference exists because the dashboard and the on-chain system calculate rankings differently.

The dashboard ranking is calculated off-chain using a defined time period (for example, averaging scores across a certain number of epochs). This gives a stable, performance-based view.

On-chain weights, however, are determined by validators through the Yuma Consensus protocol. Validators independently calculate and submit their weights, and Bittensor aggregates those submissions to determine final on-chain weights and emissions.

Because:

- The dashboard is based on score averages
- Validators independently submit weights
- On-chain aggregation follows protocol-level logic
- Time windows and normalization methods differ

…the dashboard ranking and on-chain ranking will not always match exactly.

So this is not necessarily an error — they reflect different parts of the incentive pipeline.

If there’s interest, we could also expose the actual on-chain weights or incentive values as an additional chart in the dashboard for more transparency.",2026-02-25T05:57:36.148000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,1
