1476532950886514728,1386721120652361800,𑀃・poker44・126,799672011265015819,1435366962153656420,sachhp,sachp,"Sure <@201741436117450752> 

The core problem we’re addressing is bot detection.

Modern bots no longer behave like simple scripts. They replicate human timing patterns, dynamically adjust their strategies, and can rely on real-time assistance tools. Detecting them reliably is no longer a trivial task, it requires continuous, adversarial evaluation under real conditions.

Poker44 is a decentralized integrity infrastructure built around that reality.

The platform integrates a competitive detection model directly into the gameplay layer. Validators run verifiable environments, hands are evaluated in production, and detection models are scored on previously unseen data. Everything is measurable, versioned, and auditable.

The gameplay component is not there to 'run a casino'.
It exists to generate real, evolving data within a controlled and traceable environment, which is essential for evaluating detection systems at this level of sophistication.

