1476589991814500599,1434923225229295697,ר・nepher・49,799672011265015819,1260100710649823252,nterprime,nτerprime | nepher.ai,"Hi <@&1437844197452550198> 

We are proud to announce that we have successfully completed our first **NVIDIA Isaac Lab robotics tournament**. Throughout the tournament, we achieved the goals we initially set.

### Key Outcomes

* Successfully onboarded miners and validators
* Completed the entire tournament cycle smoothly
* Verified our subnet incentive mechanism with both miners and validators in a transparent manner
* Ensured platform stability and resilience throughout a bug-free tournament, including EnvHub, miner, and validation pipelines
* Received constructive feedback on continuous validation during the contest and submission periods, and implemented it instantly
* Conducted selective invites and reviews with NVIDIA Omniverse experts

### About the Tournament

The goal of the tournament was not to develop a real-world state-of-the-art (SOTA) robotics policy. The Leatherback project serves as a proof-of-concept task within Isaac Lab. The real success of this first tournament lies not in how sophisticated the trained policy is, but in the fact that the entire pipeline functioned as expected.

