**A new [release](https://github.com/one-covenant/grail/releases/tag/v0.0.51) is out! v0.0.51**

**Breaking change.** Miners and validators must re-setup their modules from scratch. Strictly follow the updated [miner docs](https://github.com/one-covenant/grail/blob/main/docs/miner.md) and [validator docs](https://github.com/one-covenant/grail/blob/main/docs/validator.md) carefully. Many env variables have been added and to some extent many functions has drastically changed. 

- The network now trains on **Triton GPU kernel generation**. Models write optimized Triton kernels from PyTorch references instead of the previous code environment.
- **Validators** need 2 GPUs: GPU 0 for model inference, GPU 1 for kernel evaluation. New env variables: `GRAIL_GPU_EVAL=true`, `KERNEL_EVAL_GPU_IDS=1`, `KERNEL_EVAL_BACKEND=persistent`, `KERNEL_EVAL_TIMEOUT=60`. The docker-compose file has been updated.
- **Miners** can enable 3-GPU pipelined mining for ~10x throughput with `GRAIL_PIPELINE_ENABLED=true` (requires 3+ GPUs, optional but if you don't use it, you can't even generate a single group in a single window time). New env variables for pipeline mode: `KERNEL_EVAL_GPU_IDS`, `KERNEL_EVAL_BACKEND`, `GRAIL_PROOF_BATCH_SIZE`.
- Token Generation limit increased to 8k. 
- Highly optimized both validator and miner GPU memory usage to deal with 8k+ context length!
- Max rollout file size reduced to 150MB.",2026-02-27T02:58:36.829000+00:00,,False,,False,0,3,1
