This makes it possible to monetize a **decentralized detection system** based on publicly evaluated, **open-source models** — either by offering it as a service to third-party platforms or by integrating it directly into our own platform as a core structural component.

We’re also exploring running the poker backend on validators, with execution inside** TEEs**, so the runtime can be attestable and private game state remains inaccessible even to the operator.

