1478320694415724689,1354838433142542407,ᚢ・hermes・82,799672011265015819,766238622554521610,ianhe,Ian He,"Hello Hermes Community,

We have some important updates to share regarding the recent developments on our subnet and what's on the horizon. Here's what you need to know:
Recent Releases
1. Dynamic Global Burn Rate

We have implemented a dynamic global burn rate. This mechanism is designed to enhance subnet sustainability by adjusting the burn rate based on real-time conditions. The rate will now fluctuate according to miner response quality and participation levels.

Why this matters:
The dynamic global burn rate represents a more elegant and holistic approach to subnet health. Rather than relying on rigid rules or manual interventions, this mechanism creates a self-correcting economic environment where poor quality or low participation naturally leads to higher burn rates, while high-quality contributions are rewarded with more favorable conditions.
2. Miner Horde Penalty

We are introducing a measure to address concentration concerns within the subnet. Currently, this feature is disabled, but we want to be transparent about our approach.

Our Philosophy:
Hermes (SN-82) operates on a different principle than many other subnets. While other subnets leverage miners for hardware resources and capacity, our subnet asks for miner intelligence. This distinction shapes how we think about participation.

The ""Horde Penalty"" is one attempt among many we are exploring to maintain a healthy distribution of unique intelligence on the subnet. We recognize that multiple miners under the same coldkey don't necessarily add proportional value, but we also understand that addressing this requires nuance.

When activated, this penalty will start at a very small rate as we gather data and refine our approach. It is just one tool in our broader strategy—the dynamic global burn rate remains our primary mechanism for ensuring subnet health because it addresses quality directly at the source.

Upcoming
New Project Launch & Warmup Tag

We are excited to announce that the warmup tag feature has officially been released. Building on this, we will be adding a new project to the subnet very soon.

Action Required for Validators & Miners:
The upcoming project will involve a subgraph. To participate, please ensure you have configured your THEGRAPH_API_TOKEN in your environment variables. This will be essential for interfacing with the new project requirements.

Stay tuned for the official announcement regarding the project launch.",2026-03-03T09:18:39.419000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,4
