1478510217871233236,1351180661918142474,و・loosh・78,799672011265015819,1339104482524528733,agentictoaster,AgenticToaster,"Hey everyone, we just released v1.2.4 of the validator codebase. In conjunction with that we have updated the challenge api. It includes performance optimizations, some bug fixes, and some improved evaluation. We also resolved a bug where in some cases validators could be incorrectly set as inactive.

Most importantly, though, it introduces some changes to the sybil identification and scoring. The lookback period is shortened, the maximum penalty has been increased to 100% and the grace emissions has been dropped to .05%

We also significantly increased the diversity and amount of synthetic prompts. This means that identified sybil miners are recent, and miners won't be penalized for any sybil scores from before.

You should expect to see a significant number of miners drop in emissions based on this. See below for more detail.",2026-03-03T21:51:45.332000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,0
1478510317901447260,1351180661918142474,و・loosh・78,799672011265015819,1339104482524528733,agentictoaster,AgenticToaster,"## Validator:  [1.2.4] - 2026-03-02

### Improved

- **Relevance evaluation** — Improved off-topic response filtering across both single-miner and multi-miner evaluation paths.
- **Message-based challenge scoring** — Evaluation pipeline now correctly derives a scoring reference when challenges arrive in OpenAI messages format rather than as a plain prompt field.
- **Batch submission safety** — Improved handling of evaluation results when no qualifying response is available, preventing unqualified responses from being forwarded to the gateway.
- **Optimization** — Reduced timeouts and other latency driving settings.
- **Configuration** — Centralized configuration, added prior value comments.
- **Sybil Scoring** — Reduced sybil penalty minimum EMA, increased sybil penalty maximum.",2026-03-03T21:52:09.181000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,0
1478510662425772215,1351180661918142474,و・loosh・78,799672011265015819,1339104482524528733,agentictoaster,AgenticToaster,"# Sybil Detection & Scoring Update

## What Is a Sybil Attack?

A sybil attack occurs when a single operator registers multiple miners and submits the same — or effectively the same — response across all of them. Rather than contributing unique inference, they are duplicating work to collect multiple shares of the reward that should flow to genuinely distinct contributors.

This harms every honest miner on the subnet. It dilutes emissions, degrades the quality of consensus, and undermines the value the network delivers to end users.

## What We Changed

We have tightened the detection and penalty systems that identify and respond to sybil behaviour.

Detections now accumulate into a sybil score more quickly, and the consequences of a high score are more severe. Previously, confirmed sybil miners retained a portion of their weight as a grace concession. That grace period is over. Miners identified as sybils face the full penalty, up to and including complete removal from the weight distribution.

The system also now makes better use of evidence from across the validator network. Multiple validators independently flagging the same miner carries more weight than a single report.

## What This Means for You

**If you are running genuine inference, nothing changes.**

Quality, unique responses are what the subnet rewards. They always have been, and this update reinforces that. If your miners are doing real work — serving distinct, thoughtful, accurate responses — your sybil score will be zero and these changes have no effect on you whatsoever. This is true whether you are running one miner or many.

**If your miners are copying each other, stop.**

The detection system analyses response content across every miner on the network. Responses that are identical, near-identical, or structurally recycled from other miners or prior rounds are detectable. The penalty is now proportional to the severity of the behaviour, with confirmed cases resulting in complete weight removal.",2026-03-03T21:53:31.322000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,0
1478510819867365418,1351180661918142474,و・loosh・78,799672011265015819,1339104482524528733,agentictoaster,AgenticToaster,"## The Principle

This subnet exists to produce high-quality inference for real users. Every emission is a measure of value contributed toward that goal. Operators who invest in genuine inference capability well-configured models, thoughtful responses, consistent quality are the foundation of what makes this network worth using.

These changes are not a punishment for running multiple miners. They are a reaffirmation that rewards belong to miners doing real work. As sybil activity is reduced, a larger share of emissions flows to honest operators. Good work becomes more valuable.

## Disputes

If you believe you are being penalised inaccurately, you may raise a case with the team. We take false positives seriously and will review a genuine, well-documented dispute.

