1478743079371411611,1386721120652361800,𑀃・poker44・126,799672011265015819,1435366962153656420,sachhp,sachp,"Good question. I’ll take the opportunity to expand a bit and clarify how we’re thinking about this >>

We’re designing the platform with a clean and organic experience to attract real players to interact on it. Ultimately, that’s exactly what we need in order to obtain the dataset we’re looking for: **real human hands** that allow us to properly evaluate bot-detection models.

To encourage this, we’re planning a system with **real rewards (in alpha)** for winners. In an initial phase, we’re considering running **2–3 tables per day with alpha prizes**. As the platform grows and the need for data increases, we can progressively expand the number of tables.

These rewards would apply **only to the hybrid evaluation environment required by the subnet**, where **humans and bots share the same tables** to generate the dataset used for model evaluation.

In parallel, we’re also exploring the idea of creating a **sub-subnet focused on building the strongest possible poker bots**. The goal would be to create a competitive environment where participants try to develop **bots that are increasingly difficult to detect**, with rewards tied to their performance. This would continuously push detection models to improve as well. In practice, it becomes a kind of **competitive market**, where there are incentives on both sides: building the **best bot**, and building the **best model capable of detecting it**, each rewarded for their contribution.

Separately, the **main platform tables for playing with friends will not include rewards**. Those are simply meant to provide a clean and enjoyable poker experience.

Over time, we do plan to integrate a **native payment layer using smart contracts**, allowing elements like entries, prize distribution, and settlement to be handled in a transparent and verifiable way. The goal is to align the economic layer of the platform with **decentralization principles**, reducing reliance on a central operator.

That’s the long-term direction we’re building toward. We’re also fortunate to have **industry contacts willing to actively support the platform as it develops**.

Everything will come in due time ♠️♠️",2026-03-04T13:17:03.840000+00:00,2026-03-04T13:18:34.589000+00:00,False,1478607502294782044,False,0,0,1
