1478755524639199372,1375509743753236722,ⲅ・bitrecs・122,799672011265015819,644543097820151818,dimi2844,dimi,"# Bitrecs V2

All,

We're happy to announce Bitrecs V2 - a prompt evolution subnet. We have rewritten the entire subnet to function as a WTA competition for a generalized recommender prompt. There are similarities to Ridges as we took inspiration from their approach to create a robust, multi-stage evaluation pipeline. The key difference with Bitrecs is that we are evolving a prompt ""artifact"" (a yaml file) and not a python ""agent.py"". 

Our codebase is split between 2 repos:
1) bitrecs-v2 - api, validator and miner code
2) bitrecs-evals - evaluation suite

## Simple Explanation of the system:

The goal of this version is to create a SOTA generalized recommender prompt for ecommerce that will be used by our flagship shopping extension and API endpoints.

Miners create their artifact.yaml file which contains a prompt, model, provider, temperature and a few other parameters. Miners can test and tune the prompt locally using the bitercs-eval suite. Once satisfied, the miner will upload the artifact to the API for evaluation via our cli tool.

Validators fetch new miner artifacts submitted to the subnet. Each validator is expected to evaluate each miner independently and thoroughly. Each validator tracks and scores miner artifacts independently and sets weights on chain.

## Caveats of the system:

Miner artifacts are immutable .yaml files associated with a hotkey. A fresh hotkey must be registered to the subnet to submit an artifact and once a successful submission is done, that hotkey can no longer be used for subsequent submissions. Additionally, each submission must be accompanied by github GIST ID (where the artifact.yaml is stored) and an onchain extrinsic indicating an alpha burn. This is all done via our CLI (see bitrecs_cli.py)

Evaluations are done via evaluation sets (collections of evaluation tasks) along with some generic screener tasks which are always present (QoS, schema validation etc). A miner submission must pass the screeners of the generic tasks to quality for actual validator (inference heavy) evaluations.

Winners are decided via pareto scoring and dominance calculation, including threshold hurdles which must be beat in order to claim top spot. Tie breakers are settled through block_time, earlier miner submissions will win ties vs later ones.

Evaluation sets will change over time, we plan to automate their rotation to keep the system fresh and challenging.

# V2 Timeline Estimate:

March ~9 : code release and Testnet
March ~23 : Mainnet

## Subnet Features

-novel github gist storage scheme with onchain commitments
-sandboxed evaluations for isolation and consistency
-miner CLI for manual/automated submissions into the system
-fully dockerized codebase with watchtower support
-fair and distributed WTA scoring with no centralized operator overrides
-support for CHUTES & OPEN_ROUTER model selection for inference
-100% FOSS code, no hidden or black box code",2026-03-04T14:06:31.023000+00:00,,True,,False,0,0,9
