1478800333483413667,1381987595881414656,ⴷ・ⴷffine・120,799672011265015819,1457085993973841991,woof_go,Woof,"Thanks to the team for the update. This approach is a great step toward encouraging miners to focus on model improvement. With that in mind, I would also like to share a suggestion regarding the choice of the base model.

**1. Fairness**
Currently, only two miners appear to be running 27B, and those seem to be base models without significant fine-tuning. With reasonable training effort, many miners could likely reach or surpass their current performance in a short time.

In contrast, several miners have already invested substantial time and resources fine-tuning 32B models. If the system suddenly fixes on 32B, those miners would start with a significant advantage, since their pipelines and training processes are already optimized for that model.

At the same time, many other miners have spent considerable time and cost working on different models under the previous conditions. Moving directly to 32B could therefore create an uneven starting point.

Choosing 27B could help create a more neutral baseline, allowing miners to compete primarily on fine-tuning quality and optimization, rather than on prior preparation for a specific model size.",2026-03-04T17:04:34.284000+00:00,2026-03-04T17:04:47.328000+00:00,False,1478685885099937955,False,0,0,5
