1479537878265757849,1351934165964296232,ت・miid・54,799672011265015819,354083175804436481,abaza9651,Bromargiza,"The subnet operates in cycles. During each cycle, there is a window where miners attempt to submit unidentified attack vectors (UAVs). Currently, the unidentified attack vectors being tested involve different face variations. After miners submit these face variations, they are sent to a manual review process.

Once the submission window closes, the system enters a Sandbox phase for the next cycle, where a new set of unique and different unidentified attack vectors is introduced. During this time, the rewards and the manual review results from the previous cycle are finalized.

After the Sandbox phase ends, the system moves into the Execution phase. During this phase, miners receive the rewards that were determined from the previous cycle. While sending new UAVs for new Execution phase. 

You can read more about this process in our documentation, where we explain the full cycle in much greater detail. 
