1479800597673676951,1386721120652361800,𑀃・poker44・126,799672011265015819,1435366962153656420,sachhp,sachp,"The goal of the subnet **is not to generate profits by playing poker,** that’s not the point at all. The purpose is to develop and continuously improve models capable of detecting automated behavior (bots) in online poker environments.
To achieve this, we need to generate and maintain a high-quality dataset built from real hands and bot behavior, which is exactly the core problem online poker platforms face today. This data will allow us to train and continuously evaluate detection models. Btw these models will be open-source.
In addition, to foster real competition between detection models we plan to introduce an adversarial sub-subnet focused on developing increasingly human-like bots. The sole purpose of these bots is to act as controlled adversaries that push detection systems to improve.
These bots would never enter real games. **Their use is strictly internal,** within experimental and controlled environments, where they can generate high-signal data and continuously pressure detection models to better distinguish between human and automated behavior.
And in the mid-long term, the goal is to scale this system and ultimately build a decentralized online poker platform",2026-03-07T11:19:15.851000+00:00,,False,1479781244303573082,False,0,0,0
