1479815340794839150,1465362098971345010,ա・djinn・103,799672011265015819,551064429664403467,pmaymin,"Philip (Djinn, SN103)","The PSE notary timeout is a known issue: notary.pse.dev is a centralized service that gets overloaded and is rate-limited.

Good news: you don't need PSE anymore. The latest miner code uses peer notaries, other miners on the network act as notaries for each other. The validator assigns one automatically when it sends an attestation request.

Here's what to do:

Make sure you're on the latest miner code: the watchtower should auto-update, but check your version at /health endpoint. Current latest is ~v544.

Remove the TLSN_NOTARY_HOST and TLSN_NOTARY_PORT lines from your .env. The defaults handle everything. PSE is only used as a last-resort fallback now.

You don't need to compile djinn-tlsn-prover yourself. The miner auto-downloads pre-built binaries from our GitHub releases on first run (installed to ~/.local/bin/). A self-compiled binary could have version mismatches. 

Try:
rm /usr/local/bin/djinn-tlsn-prover

and let the auto-bootstrap handle it on next restart.

Make sure the notary sidecar is running. It starts automatically (check your logs for notary_sidecar_started). This lets your miner also serve as a notary for others. You should see it in djinn-miner.log.

If you still see PSE timeouts after this, it's likely just the fallback path kicking in when a peer notary fails. Those should be rare and will decrease as more miners update.",2026-03-07T12:17:50.885000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,0
