1480254828117496052,1381987595881414656,ⴷ・ⴷffine・120,799672011265015819,1429458949790371980,allan_ww,AIIan,"Hey miners! 👋

Here are the two updates to Affine

1. Scoring: Pareto Frontier Alignment Improvement
We've updated how the Pareto frontier alignment works. The scoring system now uses full partition data instead of subset-based sampling for alignment, providing larger task overlap and more accurate Pareto frontier selection. Evaluation is also simplified to single-layer only (the final combined layer), removing the previous multi-layer approach. Miners should see more consistent and fair scoring as a result.

2. New: Anti-Copy Detection Service
We've deployed an anti-copy detection service to protect original miners. It runs a periodic detection loop to identify copied models, using a two-signal voting system based on hidden states and logprob cosine similarity to detect copies with high confidence. 
Note: there may be false positives in early stages. If you believe your model has been incorrectly flagged, please share any relevant information here.

Together, these two changes aim to encourage miners to train genuinely improved models and earn more stable rewards, while reducing the pressure that copied models put on the sampling system and Chutes infrastructure — freeing up more sampling resources for original models.",2026-03-08T17:24:12.828000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,3
