1480361633640349827,1339356060787408996,כ・auτoppia・36,799672011265015819,314823554791374849,daryxx_,Daryxx,"# Road to SOTA — Weekly Update Mar 1–8

Here's what we shipped:

## ⚡ Subnet Team (Subnet & IWAP)

We completed a major refactor of the subnet as part of our open source transition — cleaning up the architecture and setting a solid foundation for outside contributors.

**Scaling & Infrastructure**
- Reduced on-chain footprint by moving detailed metadata to IPFS snapshots — leaner commitments, faster recovery
- Added IPFS integration (Hippius client) for async payload storage and retrieval
- Improved validator recovery strategy and runtime config sync between IWAP and validators

**Subnet & IWAP improvements**
- Large IWAP refactor — improved how runtime and validator information is displayed
- Added validator logs and observability improvements
- Integrated IPFS pre-consensus commitments into IWAP
- Implemented auto-updates for subnet and demo web deployments

**For miners**
- Introduced a **miner CLI** — no need to run a persistent process anymore, participation is now simpler and more flexible

---
### 🏆 Open Bounty — Hippius IPFS + S3 Integration
We've opened a bounty for this integration. If you want to contribute to the infra layer, this is a great entry point.
---

> ⚠️ Most of these changes are in `dev`, pending final review before merging into `main`.

---

## 🌐 IWA Team (IWA & Demo Websites)

The focus this week was getting the evaluation ecosystem ready for real comparisons between miners and top baseline agents.

**Evaluation & Leaderboard**
- Prepared SOTA agents to run leaderboard evaluations against season tasks — real data on how top miners stack up against the best available baselines is coming soon
- Added Sonar, code quality checks, and GitHub AI review across all repos
- Merged a large backlog of PRs and added tests to CI pipelines
- New websites staged and ready for deployment

**Operator & Agent Tooling**
- Refactored `/act` contract to follow standard conventions — easier for external devs to build on top of Automata
- Improved actions/tools interfaces and added browser extraction and evaluation utilities
- `autoppia_operator` is now public and updated to support the new contract

**Automata Ecosystem**
- Automata Cloud: authentication, user profiles, and remote browser execution taking shape
- Shipped early **Automata CLI** for local usage
- Shipped early **Automata browser extension** — focused on trajectory recording, letting users save and replay workflows

> ⏳ Full integration is waiting on a stable subnet operator.

---

## 🎨 Studio Team (Studio)
- Reviewed *PaperclipAI* and got some ""inspiration"" from it 
- Moved toward a **local-first architecture** following the OpenClaw trend
- Significant UI improvements across the board
- Vision: Full Autonomous Companies. Value proposition over other orchestration solutions is to have a marketplace of worker templates and synthetic benchmarks for company use cases. Even marketplace of whole companies. Not necessarily focus on the agents but on the evaluation and the distrubution layers.

---

🙏 Big thanks to the **Gittensor devs** for the help this week.",2026-03-09T00:28:37.249000+00:00,2026-03-10T20:29:29.726000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,3
