1480529560130027662,1381659575522033724,ⲁ・hodl-eτf・118,799672011265015819,318932875686707210,spacetime_tao,Spaceτime,"also, I'm gonna go ahead and share this concept I hinted at here https://discord.com/channels/799672011265015819/1381659575522033724/1478567643517812819. since we're fairly close to the hodl exchange launch, and it's something people can think about as trading activity increases. and it's also a benchmark that other subnets with revenue can use, which I think is pretty cool

--

Miner Equilibrium Price (MEP) is the price point at which daily net trading fees can offset 100% of daily miner emissions.

Formula:
MEP = Daily net trading fees (TAO) ÷ Daily miner Alpha emissions

Example: If HODL generates 30 TAO/day in net fees and miners earn 2,952 Alpha/day, then:
MEP = 30 ÷ 2,952 ≈ 0.01 TAO

If the current Alpha price is 0.004 TAO, the daily miner emissions are worth about 2,952 × 0.004 = 11.8 TAO—so even if miners sold everything, net fees still exceed the value of that daily supply, implying buy pressure can outweigh max daily sell pressure.

> MEP isn’t the market price—it’s a conservative reference point because it assumes miners sell 100% of what they earn.",2026-03-09T11:35:54.044000+00:00,2026-03-09T11:47:15.662000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,0
