1480550641314304033,1320739778534047785,ش・chutes・64,799672011265015819,1110466046500020325,jondurbin,jondurbin,"Yeah it's a bit unfortunate, and I really wish I could just wave a magic wand and make every single inference request free with unlimited quotas, but alas, reality is cruel, and we needed to take measures to ensure future sustainability of the subnet.

It seems most roleplay users/apps don't actually care much about TEE (or privacy in general often), so there's a bit of a disconnect there considering we have the highest levels of privacy of any inference provider now with fully open source reproducible TEE and full client-side end-to-end quantum resistent encryption etc.  But, either way, if we only have so much capacity to offer and we need to choose between paygo at full rates (or the now discounted 3%/6%/10% if you have a sub), or subscriptions at massively more than the sub price, we really have no choice but to target the paygo, and to do that we actually need capacity to meet demand.

There are really only two knobs to increase capacity - increase inventory or decrease usage.  We're working on the first, but given the GPU shortages and price increases, we also had to decrease some of the massively unprofitable usage (and we would have done this regardless because the economics of subs were bad with or without these other factors).

For example, the ""top"" user of the pro subs, when we did the analysis, used approximately ** $6,488** worth of inference (when calculated using per million token price for their actual past 30 day usage).  That's **324** times the price of the $20 sub, aka they got a **99.7% discount** on their inference.  If we are at 100% utilization on a model, and one person offers 0.003% to use a model and another user offers 100% to use a model...

It was a large shake-up, and unfortunate for those users, but the other fact is that when we did the analysis, 85% of users never exceeded that 5x cap anyways.  **85%**.  15% of users accounted for hundreds of thousands of dollars is ""losses"" (compared to paygo).  Subs are still a great value, you get up to 5x more than what you paid for the sub, AND it comes with a flat discount for any paygo usage at 3%, 6%, 10%.  There are many loud voices, but I think reasonable people still see the value.  And, keep in mind, our commodity is extraordinarily valuable - it's the most secure/private inference to my knowledge offered anywhere.",2026-03-09T12:59:40.190000+00:00,2026-03-09T13:03:32.125000+00:00,False,1480545869328679033,False,0,0,2
