1480868471683158109,1349124437752152075,م・hippius・75,799672011265015819,335489212101165056,dubsthefirst,"Dubs [τ, τ]","Miner v0.1.10: P2P Backpressure & Starvation Fixes

This release introduces critical stability patches to the Miner's networking pipeline, entirely resolving the UDP heartbeat timeouts and Out-Of-Memory (OOM) crashes that occurred when the network processed massive files.

🐛 Bug Fixes & Stability
Enforced QUIC Stream Backpressure: Relocated the payload buffer allocation and network read operations directly behind the store_sem concurrency lock in miner/src/p2p.rs. The Miner will no longer instantly buffer gigantic file payloads into memory, allowing the underlying network layer to properly throttle the Gateway.

Resolved Tokio Starvation: By stopping the unbounded flood of simultaneous chunk downloads, the Miner's core Tokio threadpool is no longer monopolized by cryptographic hashing operations. This ensures the background heartbeat task stays perfectly responsive and the Validator never drops the connection.

⚙️ Tuning & Configuration
Optimized Concurrency Defaults: Lowered the default store_concurrency from 1024 down to 16 in miner/src/config.rs. This provides a stable CPU ceiling and caps memory overhead to ~272MB per node, making it extremely resilient for deployment on shared VPS hardware.",2026-03-10T10:02:36.855000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,3
