1480931356950139084,1233428828479819876,ט・ready・33,799672011265015819,188485281148698624,papiercirer,papiercirer,"Hey, nice work getting the testing code running and digging into the scoring results. That's exactly the kind of engagement we love to see!

Your understanding is correct, but keep in mind this only applies to conversation tagging tasks which aren't 100% of the challenges.

1. Yes, the validator uses AI-generated ground truth tags.
2. Validators include a validation step that filters out conversations where no tags can be generated, so while edge cases can slip through, it's rare.
3. Correct, that's actually the intent. We want miners to generate meaningful tags for their assigned window specifically, not the full conversation. A miner won't return zero tags in practice, but if the window is sparse, the tags may not align closely with the ground truth and you'll receive a lower score. That said, it's an edge case, not the norm.

