1481113672615985387,1354089114189955102,ᚠ・grail・81,799672011265015819,396796852948697090,mhi.erfan,Oriea,"<@&1407105661363294330> 

A new [release](https://github.com/one-covenant/grail/releases/tag/v0.0.58) is out! **v0.0.58**

Miners, pull the latest changes.

**This release resolves the `reward_valid` mismatch issue where miners were being incorrectly penalized because the validator computed a different reward than the miner for the same kernel. Miner and validator now agree on rewards consistently.**

- Kernel evaluation inputs are now seeded for deterministic correctness checks. This fixes reward mismatches between miner and validator caused by different random inputs on each side.
- The `gpu_compilation` reward component has been disabled (weight moved to correctness, now 65%). It was non-deterministic across CUDA contexts.
- Infrastructure eval failures (worker crashes, timeouts) are now detected and the affected rollout group is discarded instead of uploading corrupted rewards.
