1481313737133527050,1382818027241738352,ⲅ・sundae-bar・121,799672011265015819,1443219935689183274,xrogersjohn,John,"Good manner.

I think the owner of this network is very polite and thoughtful. I also appreciate the vision you shared about building the system and community step by step.

As someone interested in ecosystem economics, I would also share one small suggestion. For some competitions, it might be good to keep submissions closed-source during the tournament. Platforms like Kaggle often do this — the work stays private while the competition is running, and then strong solutions can be shared publicly afterward.

SN 56’s mechanism also seems like a good direction. It looks like a hybrid approach between closed and open source, solving problems through tournament-style competition while still allowing knowledge to become public later. This kind of model can balance incentives, innovation, and openness in the ecosystem.

You could also divide the generalist agent problem into several smaller sub-topic tournaments and run competitions for each topic. This can make the challenges clearer, attract more specialized contributors, and gradually build stronger components for the overall system.

This approach can protect innovation during the competition while still supporting open knowledge later. It may help build a stronger and healthier ecosystem.

Wishing your SN and the whole project great success.",2026-03-11T15:31:56.411000+00:00,,False,1481308333745901810,False,0,0,0
