### Updates

**TEE**
* Updated network params.  We were seeing a low failure rate post activation for chutes ~1-2%.  It looked like network parallelism for the VM was causing issues with conntrack so reducing parallelism here should help alleviate without reducing the performance improvements too much.
* Moved raw volumes to use XFS to allow for >16TB volumes for cache.  Existing ext4 volumes are backwards compatible so you don't need to recreate your cache volumes unless you want to make them larger.
* Updated to use a base image + overlay and added a checksum verification in quick launch.  This helps alleviate a few things
  1. Occasional corruption during the download could cause bad measurements with no real indication of why.  This verifies before we hit that failure case.
  2. Ensures the VM you are launch paired with the quick launch version you are using will match measurements the validator expects for that version.
  3. As part of this we also moved images out of the repo and into `var/lib/chutes/...`
* Added a download option to help make downloading the VM updates easier.  It uses aria2c instead of curl.  For reference the image downloads for me in ~1 min.
```
./quick-launch.sh --download
```
* Added image management API.  Now you can pre-populate images hosted by the validator.  You can only download images from the validator mirror.  You can also list, prune and delete images.
```
chutes-miner tee image-[pull/list/delete/prune] ...
```",2026-03-11T16:47:13.334000+00:00,2026-03-11T16:49:29.965000+00:00,True,,False,0,0,0
1481332718015873094,1320739778534047785,ش・chutes・64,799672011265015819,389641355867062272,papermoney1163,PaperMoney,"**Chutes-Miner CLI**
* Update to support new image API endpoints for TEE nodes

**API**
* Updated to support attestation for new Chutes lib including E2E keys
* Updated to reject claiming a launch config for a Chute with lib >= 0.6.0 unless all of the miners TEE servers are >= 0.2.1
### Bugfixes
* Fixed a bug that prevented a miner from restarting the attesation-proxy in the attesation-system namespace of TEE VMs.
### Upgrade Notes
* No immediate timeline for upgrading to this latest version unless you want to take advantage of the new features and reduce the likelihood of the network issue causing a chute to be deleted when activating.
* If you want to use larger XFS volumes for cache, you need to recreate the cache volume.  Otherwise existing ext4 volumes will continue to work.
* **Important** - As we roll out the updated chutes lib, if you see 502 gateway errors when a chute activates it means the attestation proxy in the cluster is running an old image.  To resolve this you have to get the pod to restart to pull the latest image.  Due to the bug mentioned above you have options.
  1. In version 0.2.1 and 0.2.2 of the VM you will need to restart the VM so it will pull the latest image on reboot.
  2. Once upgraded to 0.2.3 you will be able to restart the pod normally using kubectl.
* To upgrade to the new image 

1. update your config
```yaml
vm:
  hostname: chutes-miner-tee-0 # Must be unique per miner hotkey
  base_image: """"  # Path to base VM image (qcow2). Empty = /var/lib/chutes/base-images/tdx-guest.qcow2
  overlay_directory: """"
```
2. Pull the image `./quick-launch.sh --download`
3. And launch like normal",2026-03-11T16:47:21.806000+00:00,2026-03-11T16:59:35.075000+00:00,False,,False,0,0,2
