1481336371980271794,1320739778534047785,ش・chutes・64,799672011265015819,1110466046500020325,jondurbin,jondurbin,"## <@&1320739375793049630>  E2EE proxy

If you want to use the full client-side quantum resistant maximum privacy/security mode chutes offers, and don't want to create your own client for doing so or use the openai client with our custom transport, you can now simply run this proxy locally and update your base URL to point there and it will handle the rest automagically.
https://github.com/chutesai/e2ee-proxy

### Running the proxy
```
docker run -p 8443:443 parachutes/e2ee-proxy:latest
```
### Client configuration
Then use this base URL for your inference:  `https://e2ee-local-proxy.chutes.dev:8443` (or with /v1 for openai clients)
`e2ee-local-proxy.chutes.dev` always resolves to 127.0.0.1, you can add an /etc/hosts override if you want to be extra sure of that.
### Anthropic format/claude code/etc.
This proxy also supports the anthropic API format for super easy integration with any claude tooling/libraries.
### OpenAI responses format
The proxy also supports the openai response format vs the normal /v1/chat/completions format, should you wish to use that format instead.
### Note on non-streaming:
Currently most models only support streaming mode, until the chutes lib has been upgraded on those models.
### Note on non-TEE models
You *can* use this proxy with E2EE encryption on non-TEE models as well, but you have to start the container with an env variable to override the default filtering:
```
docker run -e ALLOW_NON_CONFIDENTIAL=true -p 8443:443 parachutes/e2ee-proxy:latest
```",2026-03-11T17:01:52.979000+00:00,,True,,False,0,1,2
