- stop/limit price. this just means that `you don't want the alpha price to get above or below a certain level when the order is filled`. e.g. alpha price for chutes is 0.091906. if I am buying, I might not be willing for the price to get too much higher above that level. so I set a limit price at 0.092. if the alpha price gets more expensive than that, then the order does not get filled, up until the price falls below that level again. vice versa when selling. you can leave that field blank by default, if you don't necessarily care about the price swings and instead only care about slippage savings.

- good til date. keep the order open indefinitely until it gets filled, or set a hard deadline

- allow partial fills. on by default. it just means that your order can be filled via multiple tx's, rather than an all-or-nothing trade.

- public order. also on by default. you'd disable it if you want to create an OTC deal but only for a specific and private address.

when you place an order, an escrow account is generated. this is where you send the tao / alpha. it sits in this account up until someone decides to fill the order with their tao / alpha. you don't need to designate any kind of proxy. just a simple transferStake to that escrow address

usually there are trading fees, but they don't have that enabled yet. gives users time to play around with the exchange without any real costs (aside from chain tx fees)

that's the basic layout right now. the UI and UX should steadily improve over time. I'm already providing feedback to the team. the overall goal is to abstract away the complexities and make the process really simple. feel free to leave feedback if you have any",2026-03-12T09:14:57.896000+00:00,,False,1481571495380521101,False,0,0,3
