1481920086972432538,1349124437752152075,م・hippius・75,799672011265015819,335489212101165056,dubsthefirst,"Dubs [τ, τ]","## 🚀 What's New

### Reliability & Self-Healing
- **Auto re-registration** — Miner automatically re-registers with the validator after 3 consecutive heartbeat failures, without requiring a restart (#51)
- **PG assignment retry** — After re-registration, miner waits up to 60s for placement group assignment before giving up (#50)
- **Erasure shard reconstruction** — Miner can reconstruct and re-store missing shards locally for self-healing during rebalance
- **Rebalance from local doc replica** — If the validator is temporarily unreachable, miner falls back to its local iroh-doc replica for rebalance data

### Connectivity
- **Direct IP announcement at registration** — Miner now announces its direct IP address when registering with the validator, enabling faster shard transfers (previously relay-only in some cases) (#49)
- **Direct path timeout increased to 30s** — More time for QUIC direct path establishment before falling back to relay

### Rebalance Improvements
- **Concurrent adaptive shard fetching** — Rebalance now fetches shards concurrently with adaptive concurrency, significantly reducing rebalance time
- **Stability window** — Rebalance waits for network stability before starting, avoiding churn during validator reconnections
- **Dead peer skip** — Unreachable peers are skipped immediately during rebalance instead of waiting for timeout
- **Epoch history lookback** — Miner saves cluster map history across epochs for accurate rebalance even after epoch transitions

### Developer Experience
- **Cleaner logs** — Suppressed iroh internal noise (stream close errors, remote_state close events, gossip/docs noise)
- **Honest progress reporting** — Rebalance shows real shard completion percentage instead of misleading ""complete"" messages
- **CRUSH as sole stats truth** — Simplified stats pipeline, CRUSH placement is the authoritative source

### Manifest Distribution
- **iroh-doc manifest gossip** — Miner joins the validator's iroh-doc replica via ticket distributed at heartbeat, enabling near-instant manifest sync without HTTP polling

## 🔧 For Operators

No config changes required. The miner will automatically:

- Announce its direct IP on startup
- Re-register if it loses contact with the validator
- Self-heal missing shards during rebalance

> **Recommended:** ensure UDP port 11220 is open (QUIC/iroh) for best direct connectivity.",2026-03-13T07:41:21.478000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,2
