One of the strongest signals was around the importance of synthetic pipelines. This is likely one of our biggest assets. It’s something we already have that is both valuable and relatively unique. Our DevOps synthetic pipeline can be used not only for training, but also for evaluating agents, supervising them, and enabling safer execution against real infrastructure environments. This positions AlphaCore well as the ecosystem continues to mature.

Another point that came up was the importance of avoiding the sunk cost fallacy. Agentic coding is evolving extremely quickly and much of the ecosystem is open source. The opportunity here is that we can stay flexible and continue adapting our approach as the space evolves.

There is also strong momentum behind generalist agents like Codex, Claude Code, and OpenClaw. Rather than seeing that purely as competition, it also opens up an opportunity: the ecosystem is producing increasingly capable base agents that we can build on top of.

At the same time, going too niche also likely doesn’t work. A very narrow agent (for example DevOps-only) may struggle because most users will prefer agents that can handle many different types of tasks.

A promising direction is taking already strong generalist agents and making them exceptionally good at DevOps, rather than trying to build a DevOps-only agent. That approach aligns well with how the ecosystem is evolving and lets us amplify the strengths of generalist models while still focusing on real infrastructure workflows.

Another opportunity is to leverage the work already happening across the Bittensor ecosystem. Since everything is open source, there is a lot of progress across other subnets that we can build on top of instead of reinventing pieces ourselves.

We also discussed the importance of focusing on what is actually sellable. The goal is to think about what users would truly pay for and work backwards from there, rather than focusing primarily on benchmarks.

Overall, the work we’ve done on the DevOps synthetic benchmark is solid progress and gives us a strong foundation to build from. The next step is continuing to sharpen the strategy and defining more clearly what the product we’re building ultimately looks like.

Really appreciate Const taking the time to share his feedback, the conversation was extremely insightful and gave us a lot of valuable perspective.  We’re working on updating our strategy and roadmap. 

Lots of good momentum here, let’s keep building.",2026-03-13T12:27:43.140000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,4
