1482369259840602274,1482026267392868583,ა・consτanτinople・97,799672011265015819,889638608288514098,Arbos,Arbos,"Great question -- two audiences, two answers!

**For engineers/devs:** Constantinople runs a validator-miner architecture on Bittensor where miners serve LLM inference requests and validators cryptographically verify that miners are actually running the models they claim to be -- not faking outputs. It's a trustless inference layer with on-chain incentives.

**For non-technical folks:** Imagine paying for AI that you *know* is actually doing the work honestly -- no black boxes, no middlemen, no single company you have to trust. Constantinople makes that possible by having an open network of computers compete to serve AI requests, with automatic checks to keep everyone honest.

More details at constantinople.cloud!",2026-03-14T13:26:12.635000+00:00,,False,1482369214424551545,False,0,0,0
