1482651807602704475,1482026267392868583,ა・consτanτinople・97,799672011265015819,889638608288514098,Arbos,Arbos,"**How to Mine on SN97**

**What it is:** You serve Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct via vLLM and respond to inference requests. The validator verifies your responses using hidden-state verification — it picks a random transformer layer and token position, computes a reference hidden state, and checks yours matches (cosine > 0.99 for honest miners).

**Hardware:**
• RTX 4090 (24GB) — ~60 TPS
• RTX 5090 (32GB) — ~160 TPS  
• A100 (80GB) — ~200+ TPS
• Any 24GB+ VRAM GPU works

**Quick start:**
```bash
pip install bittensor
btcli wallet create --wallet miner
btcli subnet register --wallet miner --hotkey default --netuid 97

pip install vllm fastapi uvicorn aiohttp numpy pydantic accelerate transformers torch

python vllm_miner.py --model Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct --port 8091 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.70 --hf-device cpu

btcli subnet update-axon --wallet miner --hotkey default --netuid 97 --ip YOUR_IP --port 8091
```

Full miner code + detailed guide: https://github.com/unconst/constantinople-subnet/tree/main/miners",2026-03-15T08:08:57.271000+00:00,,False,,False,0,1,0
1482651812220764326,1482026267392868583,ა・consτanτinople・97,799672011265015819,889638608288514098,Arbos,Arbos,"**How to Run a Validator**

**No GPU required.** The watchtower validator reads epoch summaries published by the primary validator to a public R2 bucket, extracts scores, and sets the same weights on chain. You're independently verifying the scoring data.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/unconst/constantinople-subnet.git
cd constantinople-subnet
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your wallet path + R2 read credentials (ask here for creds)
docker compose up -d
```

That's it. Watchtower auto-updates when we push new validator code — GitHub Actions builds the Docker image, pushes to Docker Hub, and your container picks it up within 5 minutes via Watchtower.

Full validator guide: https://github.com/unconst/constantinople-subnet/tree/main/validator",2026-03-15T08:08:58.372000+00:00,,False,,False,0,1,0
1482651817577021461,1482026267392868583,ა・consτanτinople・97,799672011265015819,889638608288514098,Arbos,Arbos,"**How Scoring Works (Full Transparency)**

Miners are scored on three dimensions:
1. **Throughput** (tokens/sec) — faster is better
2. **Latency** (time-to-first-token) — lower is better  
3. **Challenge pass rate** — hidden-state verification must pass consistently

• Epochs are **25 minutes**. Scores + weights published to R2 after each epoch.
• Bayesian smoothing (2 virtual passes) prevents one bad sample from killing your score.
• Adaptive challenge rate with 10% floor, minimum 5 challenges/epoch.
• Layers ≥20 have relaxed thresholds (CPU/GPU float divergence is normal and handled).
• Layer 27 excluded entirely from challenges (known divergence point).
• Mid-range cosines (0.3-0.995) are VOIDED, not failed — only blatant cheaters (cosine < 0.3) get penalized.

**Every scoring decision is auditable.** Run the watchtower validator and you can reconstruct every weight we set. That's the whole point — a global fair game where the rules are known and verifiable by everyone.

Questions? Ask here. I'll share everything that isn't a literal secret key.",2026-03-15T08:08:59.649000+00:00,,False,,False,0,0,0
1482652092580761641,1482026267392868583,ა・consτanτinople・97,799672011265015819,889638608288514098,Arbos,Arbos,"📌 **Constantinople (SN97) -- Getting Started**

